{#
  What the numbers on this page are scoped to: which campaign, how much data
  it has, and whether every pass in it came from the same code.

  A campaign is only comparable with itself — rows from different campaigns
  were produced by different agent revisions — so the scope is stated up
  front instead of being something you'd have to infer from the URL.

  Expects `version` (selected campaign, `None` = pooled), `campaign` (its
  summary, or `None`) and `current_version`.
#}
{% if version is none %}
<div class="campaign warn">
  <strong>All campaigns pooled.</strong> These numbers average runs made
  under different agent revisions, so they aren't a fair comparison between
  models &mdash; pick a single campaign above for a rate you can report.
</div>
{% elif not campaign or not campaign.passes %}
<div class="campaign warn">
  <strong>Campaign v{{ version }} has no rows yet.</strong>
  {% if version == current_version %}
  This is the campaign new runs are written under &mdash; run
  <code>scripts/run.py run-all</code> to start filling it, or pick an
  earlier campaign above to see what's already been measured.
  {% else %}
  Nothing was ever recorded under this version.
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="campaign">
  <strong>Campaign v{{ campaign.version }}{% if campaign.is_current %}
    (current){% endif %}</strong>
  &mdash; {{ campaign.passes }} pass(es) across {{ campaign.runs }} run(s),
  {{ campaign.models | length }} model(s), {{ campaign.exercises }} exercise(s)
  {%- if campaign.first_at %}, {{ campaign.first_at[:10] }} &rarr;
  {{ campaign.last_at[:10] }}{% endif %}.
  {% if not campaign.is_current %}
  New runs are being written under v{{ current_version }}.
  {% endif %}

  <div class="revisions">
    {% if not campaign.agent_revisions %}
    Agent revision: <em>not recorded</em> &mdash; these rows predate the
    <code>agent_revision</code> column, so what code produced them can't be
    confirmed after the fact.
    {% elif campaign.agent_revisions | length == 1 %}
    Agent revision: <code>{{ campaign.agent_revisions[0] }}</code> &mdash;
    every pass in this campaign came from the same code.
    {% else %}
    <span class="flag">{{ campaign.agent_revisions | length }} distinct agent
    revisions</span> in this campaign: models did not all face the same
    Isabelle interface, so differences between them are partly differences
    in conditions.
    <ul>
      {% for r in campaign.agent_revisions %}<li><code>{{ r }}</code></li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
    {% if campaign.has_dirty_revision %}
    <div class="flag">A revision above is marked <code>-dirty</code>: it ran
    from a working tree with uncommitted changes, so it doesn't uniquely
    identify the code that produced those passes.</div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
